# Web Lesson 53 -- finite dagger structure and dagger-compact boundary.
# visual: svg
# loops: 0
# ***************************************************************************
# * PREREQUISITES -- composition, dual objects, cups, caps, compact coverage.
# * CATEGORICAL SETTING -- one finite typed process A through B to C.
# * LAW -- dagger preserves identity, reverses composition, and is involutive.
# * BOUNDARY -- one missing object dual blocks dagger compactness.
# * WHAT THIS SHOWS
# * Reverse direction and order together; then audit compact data separately.
# ***************************************************************************
;
include "lib/finite_dagger_structure.mlpl"  # reuse dagger checks
dagger_laws = u:dagger_category_laws_hold(["idA"], ["idA"], ["g*", "f*"], ["g*", "f*"], ["f"], ["f"])  # CT119
wrong_order = 1 - u:dagger_category_laws_hold(["idA"], ["idA"], ["f*", "g*"], ["g*", "f*"], ["f"], ["f"])  # COUNTEREXAMPLE
non_involutive = 1 - u:dagger_category_laws_hold(["idA"], ["idA"], ["g*", "f*"], ["g*", "f*"], ["changed"], ["f"])  # COUNTEREXAMPLE
cup_cap_compatible = u:cup_cap_are_dagger_compatible(["capA"], ["capA"])  # CT120 evidence
incompatible_cup_cap = 1 - u:cup_cap_are_dagger_compatible(["changedCap"], ["capA"])  # COUNTEREXAMPLE
coverage_missing = 1 - u:dagger_compact_coverage_is_complete([1, 0])  # CT120 boundary
disp([dagger_laws, wrong_order, non_involutive, cup_cap_compatible, incompatible_cup_cap, coverage_missing])
# ***************************************************************************
# * THE VISUAL
# * Green runs A-to-C; blue runs C-to-A with adjoints in reverse order.
# ***************************************************************************
def u:finite_dagger_structure_web_visual() { "Render the shared dagger and dagger-compact boundary visual."; u:finite_dagger_structure_visual() }  # narrated entry point
finite_dagger_structure_visual = u:finite_dagger_structure_web_visual()  # bind visual constant
finite_dagger_structure_visual  # display bound visual once
# ***************************************************************************
# * HOW TO READ THE RESULT
# * The reversed path reads g-dagger then f-dagger; applying dagger twice restores f.
# * Cup-A dagger equals cap-A, but coverage [1,0] leaves B absent.
# * THE POINT -- dagger laws are local; dagger compactness needs category coverage.
# ***************************************************************************
